{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Voice</b> — Some say: in the power that HaShem placed in nature, and likewise <i>in glory</i>. And some say: in bodies that have power." "<b>and in glory</b> — these are the mountains, as in: וְהַדּוֹרִים אֵישֵׁר (and Hazor is on the height), and on this reading הדר will be an adjective, as though he said 'among those who possess power,' in the manner of: וַאֲנִי תְפִלָּה (but I am prayer). Or its meaning is 'in power,' as written afterward: קוֹל יְהוָה שֹׁבֵר אֲרָזִים (the voice of YHWH breaks cedars)." "<b>And He mentioned the cedars</b> — because they are strong." "<b>And the meaning of 'cedars of Lebanon'</b> — they are the renowned ones among cedars."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "The second proposed reading takes the initial ב of בהדר as bet essentiae; the third defers the phrase's meaning to the next verse's content."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:56.088751061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}